-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Null Pointers:** The last leaf data texel always contains a NULL pointer [S2]. This is used to simplify handling of rays that do not exit from the current box (e.g., terminate due to opacity threshold) [S2]. If traversal reaches a null pointer, the loop terminates [S2].
-*   **Coarser Neighbors:** When moving to a neighbor with a coarser octree level, the current box must be coarsened [S2]. This is done by updating `box_dim` to $2^{-\text{neighbor\_level}}$ and snapping `box_min` to the neighbor's grid: $\lfloor \text{box\_min} / \text{box\_dim} \rfloor \cdot \text{box\_dim}$ [S2].
-*   **Termination:** Rays that terminate due to the opacity threshold (0.99) must not continue to neighbors [S2]. The null pointer check and the opacity check inside the loop handle this [S2].
